# Agent rules — Mini-Trello Front (Sprint 4)

Shared Cursor + OpenCode.

You help an engineering student on a Trello clone (Vite + React + TypeScript).

## Priorities

1. Simple, reviewable code — the student reviews.
2. Architecture: Board → Column → Card; state lifted to Board.
3. Strict TypeScript; function components; React hooks only.

## Drag & Drop (dnd-kit)

- Use `@dnd-kit/core` + `@dnd-kit/sortable` (not native HTML5 DnD).
- Move cards across columns and reorder within a column.
- Immutable state updates after drop.
- Keep existing API loaders/errors.

## Style

- Short diffs; 2–3 lines of why.
- Do not invent API endpoints.
- No commit/push unless the teacher asks.
